From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:15:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] x86/knc: early console into the host/card shared-memory
 ring

The card has no UART (SSDG 328207-002 section 4.2.2); the only path to
the host is card memory, which the host reads through the PCI aperture.
Add earlyprintk=phiring[,keep]: it locates the ring region the host
loader formatted (phi.ring=<base>,<size> on the command line, layout
per the Intel Phi 3120A ring protocol v1), validates the region and
console-channel magics, and appends printk output to the card-to-host
ring, publishing the head index after a write barrier. A full ring
drops bytes rather than stalling boot; the count is reported once the
permanent mapping is in place.

The region is mapped uncached, with early_ioremap() during setup_arch()
and re-mapped with ioremap() from an early initcall so the console can
be kept. The region header's card_boot_flags bit 0 is set on attach,
which gives the host a "kernel alive" signal before the first line, and
host_epoch_ns from the same header is exported for the wall clock.

early_ioremap() maps at most 256 KiB at a time, so the header page and
the console ring are mapped separately until ioremap() takes over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
